// Which call site reads the clock, and how often?
//
// 15.9 `clock_gettime` calls per request is the single largest syscall count on the request path
// after the hand-off was removed, and on this hypervisor it is a syscall rather than a vDSO read
// (`pvclock_clocksource_read` is 3.5% of the front-end's CPU). A count says how many; only the
// stack says why, and the difference decides whether any of it is removable: a tokio timer that is
// armed and immediately dropped, a metric that rounds a duration to microseconds, and a connection
// idle-deadline that could be coarser are three different answers.
//
// Grouped by symbol sequence in the analysis rather than here: a raw `ustack` is unique per heap
// address, so `@clk[key, ustack]` produces thousands of count-1 entries until the addresses are
// dropped.
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_clock_gettime
{
    @total[comm] = count();
    @clk[comm, ustack] = count();
}
